{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    "testFramework": "testo",
    // 4 named equivalent survivors (no ignores, no lowering):
    // - DbIdempotencyStorage.php `catch (IntegrityException) { return false; }`
    //   (Return_) and `if ($affected <= 0)` (LessThanOrEqualTo -> `< 0`), both
    //   in claim(). insert() against a real DB backend either affects exactly
    //   one row or throws IntegrityException on the unique-key conflict, so
    //   neither branch can be reached with a different outcome: dropping the
    //   catch's return falls through to `$affected <= 0` on an undefined
    //   variable, which returns false all the same. Forcing the zero-affected
    //   case would need a fake Connection double as a src-level test seam.
    // - DbIdempotencyStorage.php `$this->claimDeadlines->forget(...)` in
    //   store() (MethodCallRemoval). Dropping the spent ownership token is
    //   bookkeeping: whether or not the deadline stays in the map, release()
    //   afterwards matches no row, because the stored row is `claimed = 0` and
    //   carries the record TTL rather than the claim deadline. The only effect
    //   is the map's size in a long-running worker, which ClaimDeadlines caps
    //   anyway — there is nothing observable to assert on.
    // - RecordRowMapper.php `throw new InvalidRecordRowException(...)` removed
    //   (Throw_), in extractInt()'s isset guard. Falling through lands on the
    //   function's final fallback throw, which raises the exact same class with
    //   the byte-identical message — `sprintf('Missing or invalid column "%s"
    //   in idempotency record row', $column)` at both sites, confirmed by
    //   tightening the "missing status_code" case to an exact-message assertion
    //   and re-running: the mutant still survives because there is nothing left
    //   to assert on that differs. Killing it needs a src-side message split
    //   between the two guards, which is a behavior change out of scope for
    //   coverage-honesty work.
    "minMsi": 97,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
